  "site": "https://tuckerpaymentprocessing.com",
  "date": "2026-11-24",
  "intro": "Tucker Payment Processing was tested by independent, public security scanners. The first round found three gaps (old TLS versions still accepted, DNS not signed with DNSSEC, and no security.txt or CAA record). All were fixed the same afternoon and every scanner was run again. This summary shows both rounds.",
  "method": "Method: each scanner was run against the live site from a normal web browser on 2026-11-24. Grades, times (UTC) and check results are recorded exactly as shown on each scanner's result page; the 'Verify it yourself' links run the same scan again live. Scans run by Michael Cunningham with AI assistance (Claude).",
  "fixes_made": [
    "Cloudflare minimum TLS version raised from 1.0 to 1.2: TLS 1.0 and 1.1 are now refused (SSL Labs B to A+).",
    "DNSSEC enabled: the domain's DNS records are cryptographically signed and the DS record is published at the .com registry.",
    "CAA records added: only approved certificate authorities may issue certificates for the domain.",
    "security.txt published at /.well-known/security.txt (RFC 9116), pointing to a private GitHub vulnerability-reporting channel and SECURITY.md."
  ],
  "known_limits": [
    "internet.nl still marks two TLS 1.2 details (cipher suites; hash function for key exchange) because Cloudflare keeps some older-style options for compatibility. Choosing exact cipher suites is not available on Cloudflare's Free plan. TLS 1.3 is preferred and post-quantum key exchange is supported.",
    "Sucuri SiteCheck's malware scan was refused (HTTP 403) by Cloudflare's bot defense, which blocks automated scanners by design. Its blocklist check (9 lists) ran and is clean."
